\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I 'll praise my Maker while I've breath;
\par And when my voice is lost in death,
\par Praise shall employ my nobler power:
\par My days of praise shall ne'er be past,
\par While life, and thought, and being last,
\par Or immortality endures.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Happy the man whose hopes rely
\par On Israel's God! He made the sky,
\par And earth, and sea, with all their train:
\par His truth for ever stands secure;
\par He saves the oppressed, He feeds the poor,
\par And none shall find His promise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The Lord pours eyesight on the blind;
\par The Lord supports the fainting mind;
\par He sends the labouring conscience peace;
\par He helps the stranger in distress,
\par The widow, and the fatherless,
\par And grants the prisoner sweet release.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. I'll praise Him while He lends me breath;
\par And when my voice is lost in death,
\par Praise shall employ my nobler powers:
\par My days of praise shall ne'er be past
\par While life, and thought, and being last
\par Or immortality endures.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

